WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:03.563
This video shows how to load activities:

00:00:03.563 --> 00:00:07.686
how a filtered list of contacts becomes work for your agents, how to

00:00:07.686 --> 00:00:11.920
preview a load before you run it, and what the load reports afterward.

00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:19.654
Making one activity at a time does not scale.

00:00:19.654 --> 00:00:24.201
A load describes which contacts to pick and what work to create, and

00:00:24.201 --> 00:00:26.720
creates all the activities at once.

00:00:27.470 --> 00:00:31.081
You can count the matches before you run it, so you never call

00:00:31.081 --> 00:00:32.940
the wrong people by accident.

00:00:33.690 --> 00:00:37.921
A load runs in the background, reports who it skipped and why, and

00:00:37.921 --> 00:00:39.860
can be cloned to run again.

00:00:44.063 --> 00:00:47.846
Open Interaction Center, Management, Load Activities.

00:00:47.846 --> 00:00:53.295
The list shows the newest loads first, with their status and what they created.

00:00:53.295 --> 00:00:55.603
Click Add to start a new load.

00:00:56.055 --> 00:00:57.510
Choose the source.

00:00:57.510 --> 00:01:02.726
Manual creates activities for agents you pick, to work from the Activities list.

00:01:02.726 --> 00:01:07.942
Automatic creates unassigned activities that an AI profile works on its own, and

00:01:07.942 --> 00:01:10.065
appears with the AI features.

00:01:10.065 --> 00:01:13.765
A Dialer source appears when the outbound dialer is on.

00:01:17.964 --> 00:01:24.079
Give the load a title and pick the subject, which decides the flow of every activity.

00:01:24.079 --> 00:01:28.044
Then pick the campaign and the channel, Phone or SMS.

00:01:31.582 --> 00:01:32.866
Pick the agents.

00:01:32.866 --> 00:01:35.959
The activities are shared between them in turn.

00:01:35.959 --> 00:01:39.518
Set the urgency and instructions the agent reads first.

00:01:39.518 --> 00:01:44.537
Prevent duplicate activity with the same subject skips a contact who already has

00:01:44.537 --> 00:01:46.872
an open activity for this subject.

00:01:47.322 --> 00:01:52.223
Under Record filters, pick the record type, then narrow it by dates, time

00:01:52.223 --> 00:01:55.139
zones, a phone number filter, or a limit.

00:01:55.139 --> 00:02:00.040
Count matching records shows how many records match and how many would be

00:02:00.040 --> 00:02:04.072
loaded, with the reasons for the rest, and creates nothing.

00:02:04.535 --> 00:02:09.686
The last activity filters pick records by their last completed activity:

00:02:09.686 --> 00:02:15.829
its subject, its disposition, and its attempt, like 2+ for the second attempt or later.

00:02:15.829 --> 00:02:19.528
This is how you retry everyone who did not answer.

00:02:19.528 --> 00:02:23.425
Here no activity is finished yet, so nothing matches.

00:02:23.876 --> 00:02:25.031
Click Save.

00:02:25.031 --> 00:02:27.478
A saved load does nothing yet.

00:02:27.478 --> 00:02:29.926
It appears in the list as New.

00:02:34.127 --> 00:02:38.459
Open the row's Actions menu and choose Load activities, then confirm.

00:02:38.459 --> 00:02:42.040
You can also click Save and Load activities on the form.

00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:46.314
The status moves from Started to Loading to Loaded, and the row says

00:02:46.314 --> 00:02:50.877
how many records matched, how many were loaded, and why any were skipped.

00:02:54.953 --> 00:02:59.266
Clone makes a copy with every setting, to run again or adjust.

00:02:59.266 --> 00:03:03.009
Count matching records on the copy shows the reasons:

00:03:03.009 --> 00:03:08.083
every contact already has an open activity, so none would be loaded again.

00:03:10.771 --> 00:03:15.860
Delete removes a finished load and its report, and needs its own permission.

00:03:15.860 --> 00:03:20.515
The activities it created stay, with their assignments and schedules.

00:03:20.515 --> 00:03:23.371
To withdraw them, use Manage Activities.

00:03:27.571 --> 00:03:32.348
A load reports every matching record it did not load against one reason:

00:03:32.348 --> 00:03:36.574
an open activity for this subject, an opt out of the channel, a

00:03:36.574 --> 00:03:41.781
shared number that opted out, no address, numbers not in service, or the limit.

00:03:42.531 --> 00:03:47.321
If the server restarts during a load, it resumes by itself within about

00:03:47.321 --> 00:03:52.173
ten minutes after the last records it saved, and nobody is loaded twice.

00:03:52.173 --> 00:03:57.461
A load that keeps stopping is resumed three times, then stopped with a message.

00:03:58.211 --> 00:04:01.671
If a load fails, it goes back to New and says why, for

00:04:01.671 --> 00:04:04.439
example a dialer profile that was removed.

00:04:04.439 --> 00:04:06.631
Fix the cause and load it again.

00:04:10.831 --> 00:04:12.242
Start a campaign:

00:04:12.242 --> 00:04:16.231
load every customer in the right time zones for a call day.

00:04:16.981 --> 00:04:21.881
Retry everyone who did not answer, with the last activity filters.

00:04:22.631 --> 00:04:26.041
Share a call list fairly between several agents.

00:04:26.791 --> 00:04:31.281
Preview a list with Count matching records before anyone makes a call.

00:04:33.281 --> 00:04:37.887
Describe the contacts, check the count, load, and read the report, so every

00:04:37.887 --> 00:04:41.810
call list is built on purpose and nobody is called by accident.

00:04:41.810 --> 00:04:46.132
The user manual and the technical guide are linked in the description.

00:04:46.132 --> 00:04:47.611
Thanks for watching.

